# Embedded Learning Log - ESP32 (PlatformIO)

This repository is part of my embedded systems learning journey.  
I use it to practice core microcontroller concepts and document each experiment as I learn.

## Current Exercise

This project currently runs an ESP32 LED chaser with interactive control:

- Cycles through 6 LEDs on pins `25, 26, 27, 16, 17, 18`
- Uses PWM for LED brightness control
- Reads a potentiometer on pin `34` to set brightness in real time
- Uses a push button on pin `23` to start/stop the animation
- Prints status messages to Serial Monitor at `115200`

## Learning Goals Covered

- GPIO output and pin mapping
- PWM setup and brightness modulation
- Analog input (`analogRead`) and value mapping
- Debounced button-triggered state toggle
- Non-blocking timing using `millis()`
- Basic serial debugging and runtime visibility

## Board and Environment

- Platform: `espressif32`
- Board: `mhetesp32devkit`
- Framework: `arduino`
- Monitor speed: `115200`

Configured in `platformio.ini`.

## Run the Project (Hardware)

1. Open this project in VS Code.
2. Install the PlatformIO IDE extension.
3. Build firmware:
   - `platformio run`
4. Upload to board:
   - `platformio run --target upload`
5. Open serial monitor:
   - `platformio device monitor -b 115200`

## Wokwi Virtual Version

This is the Wokwi virtual version of this project:

https://wokwi.com/projects/462360919348337665

Use it to simulate and test the same logic when hardware is not available.

## Repository Structure

- `src/main.cpp` - main firmware logic
- `platformio.ini` - board/framework/build configuration
- `include/` - headers for future modules
- `lib/` - reusable libraries
- `test/` - test scaffolding

## Notes

This repo is intentionally iterative.  
As I learn new embedded concepts, I update the code and README to track progress.
